# fortran-names.d/2026-11-05-step44c-tab-line -- the names step 44c (tab-line.el)
# gives Lisp-derived terms, by existing rules and precedents (decided and
# reported): commands and functions verb first (R6-17, R6-40), the long
# names verb, package, rest after step 44b (decision 48 Q1:
# tab-line-close-tab -> close_tab_line_tab as tab-bar-close-tab ->
# close_tab_bar_tab), prev spelled out (no abbreviations), the hscroll
# commands from what they do (tab-line-hscroll-left -> scroll_tab_line_left,
# R6-40), predicates is_* (tab-line-tab-modified-p ->
# is_tab_line_tab_modified), and functions that give a value get_ (after
# tab-bar-tab-name-current -> get_tab_name_current).  A new name that holds
# the old one has a keep entry, as have the options named after the
# commands' words (tab_line_close_tab_function and its constants).
# tab-line-format, tab-line-tabs-buffer-groups and
# tab-line-mode-set-explicitly have no entry: each also names a variable
# that keeps its name (the buffer's tab_line_format, the option
# tab_line_tabs_buffer_groups); tab-line-hscroll neither: it also names
# the window parameter (window_tab_line_type%hscroll).
